  "principle": "Capabilities form a HIERARCHY: domain → capability → sub-capability (leaf). A leaf is what someone actually asks for ('extract a land lease', 'classify tickets', 'rerank results'); when it maps to a tunable-task method grid (architecture/tunable_task_catalog.json) it is RUNNABLE today; otherwise it is a CANDIDATE (a real unbounded/inefficient AI use we can build a grid for next). Each leaf draws on one or more TOOL PLANES (architecture/tool_planes.json) — agnostic registries of many pluggable tools the supervisor selects from to build the cheapest capability. New leaves are sourced by the discovery flywheels (mining repos/products/startups that use LLMs). serves_truth=false.",
